// Scripts the daemon runs for its clients (docs/scripting.md, "The daemon's
// script service"): the libraries it knows (shipped, per-user,
// per-project), running one as a Python host process that streams its
// output, progress and prompts, and saving the editable ones.
//
// A run is the same `revkit.script` code `rk-script` runs, started by the
// daemon with a run token that acts as the caller (its role and projects)
// and is revoked when the run ends, so the script's edits pass the normal
// authorization and provenance stamping: kind script, the script's name,
// on_behalf_of the caller, the run id as the session.
//
// A script is full Python with the rights of the daemon's user. The daemon
// runs scripts only for callers with the role --scripts-host-role names:
// editor by default when every listener is on loopback, nobody otherwise
// (docs/security.md, "Scripts").
//
// Added in api_minor 31 (feature "scripts-host"); older daemons answer
// UNIMPLEMENTED. The console (RunScriptRequest.interactive, CompleteConsole,
// CancelScriptRequest.interrupt) was added in api_minor 43 (features
// "script-console" and "script-completion").

